    <article class="doc doc-home">
      
      <section class="hero">
<p class="eyebrow">Wagyu developer docs</p>
<h1>Build private swaps into Monero</h1>
<p>One public HTTP API to quote, create and track cross-chain swaps into and out of XMR, bridge XMR to Hyperliquid as HXMR, and hand the whole flow to an AI agent. No key needed to start.</p>
<div class="hero-actions"><a class="btn btn-primary" href="/getting-started">Start the quickstart</a><a class="btn btn-glass" href="/api-reference">API reference</a><a class="btn btn-glass" href="/mcp">MCP for agents</a></div>
</section><div class="code" data-lang="bash" data-title="Quote 0.01 BTC → XMR. Try it now: no key, no account."><div class="code-head"><span class="code-title">Quote 0.01 BTC → XMR. Try it now: no key, no account.</span><button class="copy" type="button" aria-label="Copy code">Copy</button></div><pre class="shiki shiki-themes github-light github-dark" style="--shiki-light:#24292e;--shiki-dark:#e1e4e8;--shiki-light-bg:#fff;--shiki-dark-bg:#24292e" tabindex="0"><code><span class="line"><span style="--shiki-light:#6F42C1;--shiki-dark:#B392F0">curl</span><span style="--shiki-light:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#79B8FF"> -X</span><span style="--shiki-light:#032F62;--shiki-dark:#9ECBFF"> POST</span><span style="--shiki-light:#032F62;--shiki-dark:#9ECBFF"> 'https://api-beta.wagyu.xyz/v2/swaps/quote'</span><span style="--shiki-light:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#79B8FF"> \</span></span>
<span class="line"><span style="--shiki-light:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#79B8FF">  -H</span><span style="--shiki-light:#032F62;--shiki-dark:#9ECBFF"> 'content-type: application/json'</span><span style="--shiki-light:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#79B8FF"> \</span></span>
<span class="line"><span style="--shiki-light:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#79B8FF">  -d</span><span style="--shiki-light:#032F62;--shiki-dark:#9ECBFF"> '{"fromChainId":20000000000001,"toChainId":0,"fromToken":"bitcoin","toToken":"XMR","fromAmount":"1000000"}'</span></span></code></pre></div>
<div class="facts"><div class="fact"><b>11</b><span>chains in the catalog</span></div><div class="fact"><b>16,572</b><span>tokens you can send</span></div><div class="fact"><b>$1.52B</b><span>swapped, all time</span></div><div class="fact"><b>5,432</b><span>orders, all time</span></div></div><p><em>Live from the API, read when this page was built (24 Nov 2026, 15:11 UTC).</em></p>
<h2 id="start-here"><a class="anchor" href="#start-here" aria-label="Link to this section">#</a>Start here</h2>
<div class="cards"><a class="card" href="/getting-started"><span class="card-icon"><svg class="icon" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M15.914 4a1.5 1.5 0 00-2.474-1.561l-9 9A1.5 1.5 0 005.5 14h4.002a.5.5 0 01.471.666L8.086 20a1.5 1.5 0 002.475 1.56l9-9A1.5 1.5 0 0018.5 10h-3.997a.5.5 0 01-.472-.667z"/></svg></span><strong>Quickstart</strong><span>Quote, create and track a swap in four calls.</span></a><a class="card" href="/authentication"><span class="card-icon"><svg class="icon" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M2.586 17.414A2 2 0 0 0 2 18.828V21a1 1 0 0 0 1 1h3a1 1 0 0 0 1-1v-1a1 1 0 0 1 1-1h1a1 1 0 0 0 1-1v-1a1 1 0 0 1 1-1h.172a2 2 0 0 0 1.414-.586l.814-.814a6.5 6.5 0 1 0-4-4z"/> <circle cx="16.5" cy="7.5" r=".5" fill="currentColor"/></svg></span><strong>API keys and fees</strong><span>Get a key in two minutes and earn 0–5% on every order you send.</span></a><a class="card" href="/mcp"><span class="card-icon"><svg class="icon" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M12 8V4H8"/> <rect width="16" height="12" x="4" y="8" rx="2"/> <path d="M2 14h2"/> <path d="M20 14h2"/> <path d="M15 13v2"/> <path d="M9 13v2"/></svg></span><strong>MCP server</strong><span>Give Claude, Cursor or any MCP client a swap tool.</span></a><a class="card" href="/native-bridge"><span class="card-icon"><svg class="icon" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M8 3 4 7l4 4"/> <path d="M4 7h16"/> <path d="m16 21 4-4-4-4"/> <path d="M20 17H4"/></svg></span><strong>Bridge XMR to HXMR</strong><span>Move XMR to Hyperliquid as HXMR and back.</span></a><a class="card" href="/chains"><span class="card-icon"><svg class="icon" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M10 13a5 5 0 0 0 7.54.54l3-3a5 5 0 0 0-7.07-7.07l-1.72 1.71"/> <path d="M14 11a5 5 0 0 0-7.54-.54l-3 3a5 5 0 0 0 7.07 7.07l1.71-1.71"/></svg></span><strong>Chains and tokens</strong><span>Every chain, chain id, minimum and token value, live.</span></a><a class="card" href="/api-reference"><span class="card-icon"><svg class="icon" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M12 5v16"/> <path d="M20.001 19A2 2 0 0022 17V5a2 2 0 00-1.999-2L16 3.002A5 5 0 0012 5a5 5 0 00-4-2H4a2 2 0 00-2 2v12a2 2 0 001.999 2H8a5 5 0 014 2 5 5 0 014-2z"/></svg></span><strong>API reference</strong><span>Every route, generated from the live contract.</span></a></div><h2 id="how-a-swap-works"><a class="anchor" href="#how-a-swap-works" aria-label="Link to this section">#</a>How a swap works</h2>
<ol>
<li><strong>Pick the two assets.</strong> Each asset is a <code>chainId</code> plus a token value from the catalog (<a href="/chains">Chains and tokens</a>).</li>
<li><strong>Quote.</strong> <code>POST /v2/swaps/quote</code> returns what the user would receive. It is an estimate, not a deposit instruction.</li>
<li><strong>Create the order.</strong> <code>POST /v2/swaps</code> returns a deposit address, the exact amount to send, a deadline, an <code>orderId</code> and a private <code>sessionId</code>.</li>
<li><strong>Track it.</strong> Poll <code>GET /v2/swaps/{id}</code> with the session, or listen on a WebSocket, until the order is <code>completed</code>, <code>refunded</code>, <code>failed</code> or <code>expired</code>.</li>
</ol>
<p>The user sends funds from their own wallet. Nothing moves until that deposit arrives. The <a href="/getting-started">quickstart</a> walks through the four calls with real responses.</p>
<h2 id="five-rules-that-prevent-most-bugs"><a class="anchor" href="#five-rules-that-prevent-most-bugs" aria-label="Link to this section">#</a>Five rules that prevent most bugs</h2>
<ul>
<li><strong>Amounts are integer strings in atomic units.</strong> <code>&quot;1000000&quot;</code> is 0.01 BTC (8 decimals). Never send a float. See <a href="/money-and-settlement">Amounts and fees</a>.</li>
<li><strong>Show the funding instruction, not the quote.</strong> After creating an order, display its <code>depositAddress</code>, <code>depositAmount</code> and <code>expiresAt</code> exactly as returned.</li>
<li><strong>Never retry order creation automatically.</strong> There is no idempotency key: a second <code>POST /v2/swaps</code> after a timeout can create a second order.</li>
<li><strong>Keep the <code>sessionId</code> private.</strong> It is the only credential that can read or act on an order. Send it in the <code>X-Session-ID</code> header, never in a URL.</li>
<li><strong>Drive your screen from <code>customerState</code>.</strong> It says what the user sees and may do next. <code>status</code> is the coarse outcome. See <a href="/order-lifecycle">Order lifecycle</a>.</li>
</ul>
<h2 id="where-things-live"><a class="anchor" href="#where-things-live" aria-label="Link to this section">#</a>Where things live</h2>
<div class="table-wrap"><table>
<thead>
